oeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"fb31cb3610914947792d87b655df9f6a929b81d9239965feb527862f0e4655dc","event_uuid":"efbdf729-4606-4774-8098-592e1e30fce7","position":{"commit_sha":"572624aaebda35d10f71adaa19f58c9df0fcba1d","position":"1795087062218034632-efbdf729-4606-4774-8098-592e1e30fce7"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause per signature, read from the Windows sweep job logs of runs 43820680079, 43871224211 and the b4e0d01b649 scheduled run (2026-11-15/16):\n\n1. Read-only git objects (tests): git writes loose objects and packs read-only; Windows refuses to delete a read-only file (`PermissionError: [WinError 5] Access is denied: '...\\.git\\objects\\b0\\45b0...'`). Sites: `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py:318` (`_plant_poison`), `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py:517`, `tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py:674,701,717,765`. `test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py::test_completed_snapshot_test_leaves_basetemp_removable` fails the same way inside `shutil.rmtree(basetemp)` on the nested run's `repo\\.git\\objects\\...`, not on the rebar snapshot the test is about.\n2. Concurrent replace onto one target (product): `os.replace` raises `PermissionError` (WinError 5) on Windows while another rename or handle holds the target. 5 tests; fixed at class level by sporting-feudalist-bluet (shared `fsutil.replace_with_retry`), which removes those 5 lines.\n3. POSIX-only interprocess locks with a fallback that breaks on Windows (product): `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py:60-91` `interprocess_lock` uses `fcntl.flock` and otherwise an `os.mkdir` spin-lock; on Windows the `mkdir` of a lock dir another thread is removing raises `PermissionError` (`...\\locks\\bytes.total.lock.d`, `...\\index.sqlite3.recover.lock.d`), failing `test_snapshot_cache.py::test_add_bytes_atomic_under_concurrency` and `test_similar_tickets_index.py::test_only_one_caller_discards_when_two_enter_recovery_on_one_stale_index`. `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py:14-17,51-59` takes no lock at all on Windows, and the CRT's append mode is seek-then-write, so concurrent appends overwrite each other (`Expected 50 lines, got 46`). `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:345-360` has the same mkdir guard.\n4. Rename of a directory holding an open file: `test_snapshot_cache.py::test_open_reader_survives_eviction_then_relookup_misses` renames a live snapshot entry while a reader holds a file in it (`:159`, WinError 5). Windows forbids that rename; the product already handles it, `_evict` returns 0 and keeps the entry (`src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:210-213`), so the reader is safe. The test encodes POSIX delete-on-last-close only.\n5. Deleting a process's cwd: `test_detached_child_cwd.py::test_durable_cwd_never_raises_when_the_callers_own_directory_is_gone` rmtrees its own cwd (WinError 32). Windows never lets a directory in use as a cwd be deleted, so the state the test reaches cannot occur there.\n6. Hidden `.git` file: `test_copied_worktree_guard.py:165` rewrites a linked worktree's `.git` file with `write_text` (`[Errno 13] Permission denied`). Git for Windows marks `.git` hidden (`core.hideDotFiles`), and `CreateFile(CREATE_ALWAYS)` on a hidden file fails with access denied.\n7. `tests/scripts/reducer/test_reducer_cache.py::test_cache_invalidated_on_file_deletion` failed 1 of 3 on an mtime equality assertion that main has since replaced with an inode/content check (bug d45f-229f-effe-4cf8, `:201-206`).","timestamp":1795039237640746773},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed as Gerrit 3439 (1fa2f61915b, on top of the merged replace-retry change 6f5f854be4c from sporting-feudalist-bluet). make verify passed in full (exit 0) with the integration tier (226 passed, 2 skipped). The new `.append.lock` sibling carries a `mechanism-ok: lock` marker: it replaces an in-file fcntl flock Windows lacks. Portability: lock_kernel selects fcntl or msvcrt; the test changes use os.chmod with stat.S_IWRITE, valid on both.","timestamp":1795053290597293723},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Seen in test.yml run 44456347985 at ab323f7df0c (2026-11-18 PST), job `sweep (windows)` 135332660982: `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py::test_a_git_failure_captures_object_store_forensics` failed with \"the .git/objects listing must show the objects that DID survive\". The test's `_unlink_git_object` helper was changed today in 035b7371de8 for read-only git objects, and the object-listing assertion is what fails afterwards. This is reported here because it falls in this ticket's class. Not investigated further from cluster D.","timestamp":1795066268671797762},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged as 035b7371de8 (Gerrit 3439). First Windows sweep with it, run 44456347985 (job 135332660982): every removed file-locks line passed or skipped except 2, each masked before by the first failure. `test_snapshot_cache.py::test_open_reader_survives_eviction_then_relookup_misses` read `b'content\\r\\n'` (Windows git checks text out with CRLF); `test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py::test_a_git_failure_captures_object_store_forensics` looked for `xx/yyyy` but the test helper printed Windows separators. Both are test-side; fixed in follow-up Gerrit 3444 (991c22ca637); make verify passed in full, integration tier 226 passed.","timestamp":1795072425067381844},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Sweep 1 of 3 after the follow-up: run 44487190183 (job 135433617476, main at 3f47117c97b, 2026-11-19). Every line removed from `file-locks.args` (now deleted) passed; none is among the run's 13 failures. The job concluded `failure` on 13 tests from other classes (separator and guard tests on arctic-unsecular-esok / obtuse-phenocryst-verdin, a bd66 worker crash on powderblue-effectual-racerunner).","timestamp":1795081735877559006},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Sweep 2 of 3: run 44503581058 (job 135490319213, main at 92d3f373e2c, 2026-11-19). Every test formerly in `file-locks.args` passed again; the job's 14 failures all belong to other classes (arctic-unsecular-esok, obtuse-phenocryst-verdin, and 2 new `test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py` cases). Handoff: needs one more sweep with these tests passing and the job concluding `success`, which waits on the other classes. Close as `env_integration` then.","timestamp":1795087062218034632}],"created_at":1794857688422460321,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"83dbfb61-fc41-4746-89f6-f9bf11b5d43f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"},{"link_uuid":"55e281b5-8ec7-4819-a3c5-0facee9a0ff4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f59a-4c53-9452-4d3f"},{"link_uuid":"af852e20-cd5b-4a7e-9b44-efe994d92e60","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f508-53d4-1602-4f8e"},{"link_uuid":"cb4435a8-ebb9-4367-b04a-2cc52a258be8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"52e8-609a-3cde-44bf"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects tests known to fail on Windows through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/file-locks.args`. This bug owns that file: 19 tests in 15 modules. The root cause per signature, with the log evidence, is in the ticket comment \"Root cause per signature\"; in short: git's read-only objects cannot be deleted on Windows (tests); `os.replace` onto a contended target raises `PermissionError` (product, 5 tests); `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py:62-91` `interprocess_lock`, `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py:14-17,51-59` and the `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:355-366` guard use `fcntl` with no working Windows lock (product); one test renames a directory holding an open file; one deletes its own cwd; one rewrites git's hidden `.git` file; and one (`test_reducer_cache.py`) failed on an mtime assertion main has since replaced.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix product locks through the portable lock leg the store already uses, and make the tests stop assuming POSIX filesystem semantics where the behaviour under test does not depend on them.\n\n- Concurrent replace (5 tests: `test_unique_cache_writes.py::test_two_concurrent_writers_to_one_target_both_publish`, `test_completion_verdict_cache.py::test_concurrent_persist_for_same_criterion_loses_no_writer`, `test_plan_review.py::test_concurrent_save_checkpoint_same_digest_loses_no_writer`, `test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py::test_peer_confirmations_distinct_concurrent_saves_are_merged`, `test_mcp_gate_async.py::test_follower_start_does_not_reclobber_the_leaders_index_record`): fixed and removed from `file-locks.args` by sporting-feudalist-bluet's change. This ticket's change is pushed after that change merges and rebases onto it.\n- Locks: `interprocess_lock` takes `rebar._store.lock_kernel.take_blocking_exclusive` on the opened lock file and releases with `release_exclusive` (`src/rebar/_store/lock_kernel.py:120-182`, Windows `msvcrt` leg included). The `mkdir` spin fallback is removed: every supported platform has a kernel leg, and `lock_kernel` raises `NoExclusiveLegError` rather than degrade. `alert_store.append` serializes through `rebar._store.fsutil.sibling_exclusive_lock(today, lock_name=\".append.lock\")` (`src/rebar/_store/fsutil.py:33-63`); retention ignores dotfiles (`src/rebar/reconciler/scratch_retention.py:84`). The janitor's non-blocking GC guard uses `lock_kernel.take_exclusive` and `is_contention`.\n- Read-only objects: clear the read-only bit (`os.chmod(p, stat.S_IWRITE | stat.S_IREAD)`) before each `unlink` at the test sites listed in the comment. In `test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`, `shutil.rmtree(basetemp, onexc=...)` clears the bit and retries only for paths inside a `.git` directory and re-raises everything else, so the test still proves the rebar snapshot itself is removable.\n- `test_snapshot_cache.py::test_open_reader_survives_eviction_then_relookup_misses`: on Windows assert the platform's semantics, the eviction rename is refused while the reader holds the file, the reader still reads the content, and after close the entry evicts and a relookup re-heals; POSIX keeps the delete-on-last-close assertion.\n- `test_detached_child_cwd.py::test_durable_cwd_never_raises_when_the_callers_own_directory_is_gone`: `skipif(os.name == \"nt\")`, reason \"Windows refuses to delete a directory that is a process's cwd, so this state cannot occur there\".\n- `test_copied_worktree_guard.py:165`: unlink the `.git` file before writing it (git for Windows marks it hidden).\n- `test_reducer_cache.py`: remove the line; the current assertion (`:201-206`) is portable, and the sweep runs prove it.\n- Delete `file-locks.args` and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty.\n\nPortability: the new lock paths use `lock_kernel`, which selects `fcntl` or `msvcrt`; the test changes use `os.chmod` with `stat.S_IWRITE`, valid on both. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py`, `src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py`, `tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py`, `tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py`, `tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py`, `tests/unit/test_snapshot_cache.py`, `tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_copied_worktree_guard.py`\n- `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/file-locks.args` (deleted), `.github/workflows/test.yml`\n\n## Testing\n\n- POSIX: the touched tests and the existing lock tests (`test_snapshot_cache.py` cross-process single-flight, `test_similar_tickets_index.py`, `test_alert_store_concurrency.py`, janitor GC tests) pass under `make verify`. Failure path: a held GC guard still yields `GcResult(skipped=\"locked\")` (existing janitor test).\n- Windows: 3 consecutive dispatched `sweep (windows)` runs on main after the merge.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded per signature on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes on the change.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `file-locks.args` names a test that passed in 3 consecutive `sweep (windows)` runs on main after the fix (run ids recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on those runs, with `file-locks.args` and its `@` reference removed.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/git_fetch.py","reason":"interprocess_lock through lock_kernel"},{"path":"src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py","reason":"GC guard through lock_kernel"},{"path":"src/rebar/reconciler/alert_store.py","reason":"append serialized through sibling_exclusive_lock"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py","reason":"clear read-only bit before unlink"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py","reason":"clear read-only bit before unlink"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pinned_ticket_view.py","reason":"clear read-only bit before unlink"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py","reason":"rmtree onexc for git objects only"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_snapshot_cache.py","reason":"Windows eviction semantics"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py","reason":"skip impossible state on Windows"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_copied_worktree_guard.py","reason":"hidden .git file rewrite"},{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/file-locks.args","reason":"deleted once empty"},{"path":".github/workflows/test.yml","reason":"drop the file-locks argfile reference"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","52e8-609a-3cde-44bf"],["relates_to","f508-53d4-1602-4f8e"],["relates_to","f59a-4c53-9452-4d3f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"a7fcca8a-2adc-4846-a022-08bcc3811815","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"b8dd-85be-1dbb-45b9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: open handles, read-only git objects and concurrent replace raise PermissionError (19 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["55e281b5-8ec7-4819-a3c5-0facee9a0ff4","0c4059ce-a260-455d-8089-45c778346559","402a95b7-4f1f-4d67-b4e5-b3f5b4e70b45","33393a52-43c7-4ce7-859e-b645adb818db","992ff070-71a7-4daa-9fef-638c97ac8a14","a7fcca8a-2adc-4846-a022-08bcc3811815","1eea56b0-8490-4f45-b52e-6aaa4d2a1fbe","8bf5bcce-ea44-4592-9c5c-5de19f74f9af","af852e20-cd5b-4a7e-9b44-efe994d92e60","ebc141f5-8769-4c4e-9319-6d468f8a8b35","3eef7bfb-1d0b-46f7-acb0-32a1402e9990","cb4435a8-ebb9-4367-b04a-2cc52a258be8","e673c094-8f6a-4b4e-ac33-c06c86ef00dc","efbdf729-4606-4774-8098-592e1e30fce7"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795087062218034633,"uuid":"fe95afbf-6caf-4a54-8995-fe779da43f29"}
